  "source_and_output_review": [
    {
      "rule": "Reported local sessions may establish an anonymous first session but cannot replace a preassigned or previously discovered owned identity before caching, replay or native continuation.",
      "files": [
        "lib/execution.mjs",
        "lib/execution_io.mjs",
        "lib/control.mjs",
        "lib/task_prepare.mjs",
        "lib/tick.mjs",
        "lib/commands/resume.mjs"
      ],
      "boundaries_checked": [
        "Local settlement validates the adapter session using ownsProviderSession before writing result.json or adopting session/cost/outcome metadata.",
        "Fresh collection and saved-cache replay validate local session ownership. Omitted IDs retain the owned session; malformed or foreign reported IDs raise EXECUTION_RESULT without a new cache or dispatch.",
        "Read-only sessionFrom validates both cached and parsed local identities. Legacy continuation uses the recorded registry session; acknowledgement snapshots anchor preassigned sessions even after pre-fix current/cache corruption.",
        "Local control interrupt and task preparation use the boundary session reader when available, preserving legacy raw-runner fallbacks.",
        "Claude and Gemini preassigned sessions and continued Codex/OpenCode sessions reject foreign IDs. Goose emits no session ID and keeps its preassigned identity. Initial anonymous Codex/OpenCode runs may discover their session normally.",
        "Settlement, collection, cancellation-before-collection, replay and restart retain ownership and deny a foreign continuation; restoring exact owned evidence permits collection without a replacement dispatch.",
        "Remote session ownership, acceptance recovery, operation idempotency, result artifact validation and private log retention retain their existing contracts."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "local settlement, collection and cached replay reject foreign sessions before adopting results",
        "local session ownership rejects malformed IDs and retains omitted IDs or first discovered sessions",
        "legacy local session readers cannot redirect continuation away from the recorded registry session"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rule": "A stopped task and its provider run are separate facts: natural terminal completion ends cancellation waiting without claiming a provider stop or rewriting a collected outcome.",
      "files": [
        "lib/execution.mjs",
        "lib/control.mjs",
        "lib/tick.mjs",
        "lib/task_prepare.mjs",
        "docs/execution.md"
      ],
      "boundaries_checked": [
        "Already collected remote success/failure returns confirmed:false, terminal:true, keeps the future-dispatch fence and quarantine, and performs no transport cancellation.",
        "Cancellation no longer replaces the recorded exit of an already collected terminal result. Success/failure, completion time, session, known cost and cached result survive restart and registry settlement.",
        "Operator cancellation and remote timeout share cancellationStatus. Confirmed provider cancellation, already-ended work and unconfirmed live stops retain distinct truthful receipts.",
        "Periodic/startup reconciliation repairs applied pending receipts after natural completion, only for the exact recorded stop_run or legacy last.run. An unrelated terminal root cannot satisfy the request.",
        "A pending cancellation that naturally ends is quarantined without collection or publication. Existing preparation recovery already accepts confirmed or terminal cancellation metadata.",
        "Unsupported/unknown-acceptance stops, pending/retried cancellation keys and local timeout recovery remain unchanged; no replacement paid work or independent read-only polling is introduced."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "remote terminal cancellation controls finish without claiming a provider stop and preserve collected outcomes",
        "terminal control reconciliation ignores an unrelated completed root",
        "natural completion after a pending stop quarantines results without claiming cancellation",
        "cancellation after a contradictory terminal inspection quarantines the known completed root without a stop call",
        "a stop during failed result retrieval quarantines the completed root without a cancellation call",
        "a stop after collected terminal results quarantines both success and failure caches"
      ]
    }
  ],
